    {
      "id": "5759a464-e088-46db-ada3-5986efb9f997",
      "name": "About this inventory",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -20,
        -480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 720,
        "height": 700,
        "content": "## Who is this for?\nOperations teams and Famulor workspace administrators who want a weekly overview of their AI assistants in Google Sheets.\n\n## How it works\nEvery Monday at 09:00, or on a manual run, the workflow reads assistants through the Famulor API. It checks pagination and prepares nine inventory fields. Google Sheets appends or updates rows by Assistant ID, preserving unrelated columns such as Owner and Review notes. Preview only starts enabled, so you can inspect the rows before writing. Prompts, tools, recordings and contact details are not copied to the sheet. Deleted assistants remain in the sheet; Last seen helps identify older entries.\n\n## Setup\n1. Select an n8n HTTP Header Auth credential in Read Famulor assistant pages. Use Authorization as the header name and Bearer followed by your Famulor workspace API key as its value. The key needs assistants:read. Check the selected credential after import.\n2. Create these sheet headers: Assistant ID, Name, Active, Mode, Speech language, Tags, Created at, Updated at, Last seen. Select your Google Sheets credential, spreadsheet and tab.\n3. Set your workflow timezone; the default is Europe/Berlin. Run a manual preview, then turn Preview only off and activate the weekly schedule.\n\n## Requirements and customization\nUses built-in n8n nodes and Google Sheets edit access. Incomplete, capped or inconsistent scans stop before writes; the default limit is 2,000 assistants. Customize the schedule and mapping. Restrict sheet access and execution-history access: API responses can include configuration fields even though the sheet excludes them. Concurrent sheet writes are not transactional. [Famulor setup guide](https://docs.famulor.io/automations/n8n)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
